## Task 4: Multi-line Strings

### Literal Block Style (|)
- Preserves all line breaks exactly as written.
- Best for scripts, configuration files, certificates, or logs.

### Folded Block Style (>)
- Converts line breaks into spaces.
- Best for long descriptions, documentation, or paragraphs.

### When to use `|` vs `>`?

- Use `|` when formatting and line breaks must remain unchanged (e.g., Bash scripts, SQL queries, configuration snippets).
- Use `>` when you want to write readable multi-line text in the YAML file but have it treated as a single paragraph when parsed.


